    <briefdescription>
<para>CHANNELS. </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>A base structure for an IPC message.</para><para>A message at any moment can be either:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>new</para></listitem><listitem><para>in a channel, waiting to get delivered</para></listitem><listitem><para>delivered</para></listitem></itemizedlist>
</para><para>When a channel is destroyed, all messages buffered by the channel must be destroyed as well. The destroy callback is therefore necessary to free any message-specific resources in case of delivery failure. </para>    </detaileddescription>
